    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In all the work which has been reported on pulse-testing, the pulse and shut-in periods are equal. The effect of unequal periods on pulse-testing was not studied. It would be useful to find out the response of pulse-tests when the ratio between the pulse period and the shut-in period is not one. This will enable the use of pulse tests without limitations on the length of the different periods and will determine the optimum ratio between the pulse and the shut-in periods which gives the maximum pulse-test response.There is only one article in the literature which gives enough information so that an engineer can design and analyze pulse- 3 tests. This article is somewhat limited, because beside assuming that the pulse and shut-in periods are equal, it also assumes that all time lags are equal. The design and analysis of pulse-tests without these assumptions has not been studied.This research was carried out to fill these existing gaps in knowledge about the behavior of pulse-tests. The effect of unequal periods on pulse-testing was studied. Curves and equations to design and analyze pulse tests were produced for cases where the pulse and shut-in periods are not equal without assuming that the time lags are equal.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
